    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d149">

                <pb facs="0373" n="341" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v02/pg341"/>

                <head>149. Memorandum for the Record<anchor n="1" xml:id="d149-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1965-02-20">February 20,
                        1965</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the NSC meeting on February 18, 1965,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d149-f2"/> the
                    President gave approval to the line of policy outlined in London 5147 to
                    Ambassador Bruce dated February 16,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d149-f3"/> with the
                    following exceptions: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The President made no decision with respect to any call for a meeting
                            of the UN Security Council or other discussion in the Security
                            Council.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The President made no decision with respect to the means or frequency
                            of reports on U.S. military action.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>The President made no decision within the meeting with respect to the
                            timing of the next military action.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>A copy of telegram 5147 to London is attached as a document of reference. The
                    President read from the document, with the exceptions noted, in presenting this
                    matter to the Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">McGeorge Bundy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
